    {
      "id": "F6Wp7DU4ZKArxRtLSc8ME",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3297.867123476658,
      "y": 4389.64688738882,
      "width": 1641.2989501953125,
      "height": 825,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 97072708,
      "version": 2536,
      "versionNonce": 118207740,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785894975450,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Alternate design for location specific forecast\n\nIn this new design, the user does provide a piece of location data.\n\n## High level architecture\n\nHandler\n    Forecast Fetcher\n        Check Cache\n        If cache is missing, check circuit breaker if closed, get lock for that location, fetch data from weather APIs \n                If request fails, increase failure count and return error or Stale data (business decision)\n                    If failure count \n                    \n    Circuit Breaker\n        Inform of Error: \n            Increment count of errors\n            \n            If retry header is present, save this, change state to opened regardless of error count\n    \n            If state is half opened OR ErrorCount > threshold, change to opened\n\n        Check if allowed\n            If closed, return true\n            If half opened, return false\n            If opened, check cooldown period, if time since last tripped is bigger than cooldown, allow 1 routine (with a compare and swap) and change state to half open.\n\n        Leak errors over time\n\n        Inform Of Success, set error count to 0, if opened / half opened, change to closed\n\n    Forecast Cache\n    \n    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Alternate design for location specific forecast\n\nIn this new design, the user does provide a piece of location data.\n\n## High level architecture\n\nHandler\n    Forecast Fetcher\n        Check Cache\n        If cache is missing, check circuit breaker if closed, get lock for that location, fetch data from weather APIs \n                If request fails, increase failure count and return error or Stale data (business decision)\n                    If failure count \n                    \n    Circuit Breaker\n        Inform of Error: \n            Increment count of errors\n            \n            If retry header is present, save this, change state to opened regardless of error count\n    \n            If state is half opened OR ErrorCount > threshold, change to opened\n\n        Check if allowed\n            If closed, return true\n            If half opened, return false\n            If opened, check cooldown period, if time since last tripped is bigger than cooldown, allow 1 routine (with a compare and swap) and change state to half open.\n\n        Leak errors over time\n\n        Inform Of Success, set error count to 0, if opened / half opened, change to closed\n\n    Forecast Cache\n    \n    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
